{% doc %}
  A row of stars for a rating a merchant typed, rather than one a review app
  stored.

  ## Why this is not `snippets/rating.liquid`

  That one reads `product.metafields.reviews.rating` and renders nothing when
  the metafield is missing, which is the right behaviour for a product: a store
  with no review app should show no rating, not "0 out of 5".

  This one is handed a number. It is what a testimonial's own star row needs —
  the merchant typed 4, so four stars — and what the placeholder state of a
  product card needs, where there is no product to read a metafield off yet.
  Both used to draw their own `for` loop; `blocks/testimonial.liquid`'s drew
  five identical glyphs because the `class:` argument it passed was the loop
  index rather than a comparison against the rating.

  ## The stars are decoration and the number is the content

  Five star glyphs read aloud are five identical words with no number attached,
  so the row is `aria-hidden` and the rating is announced as the same translated
  sentence `snippets/rating.liquid` uses. `announce: false` turns that off for
  the one case where it is noise — a second star row inside a card that has
  already announced its rating.

  Halves are drawn at the same 0.5 threshold as `snippets/rating.liquid`, so a
  4.5 typed here and a 4.5 stored by an app produce the same row.

  @param {number} rating - 0 to `max`. Renders nothing at 0 or below.
  @param {number} [max] - Default 5
  @param {number} [size] - Pixel size of one star. Default 14
  @param {string} [class] - Extra classes on the wrapper
  @param {boolean} [announce] - Emit the visually hidden sentence. Default true

  @example
    {% render 'rating-stars', rating: block.settings.rating %}

  @example
    {% render 'rating-stars', rating: 5, size: 12, announce: false, class: 'testimonial-card__info-stars' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign scale_max = max | default: 5 | plus: 0
  assign value = rating | default: 0 | times: 1.0
  assign star_size = size | default: 14 | plus: 0

  assign say_it = true
  if announce == false
    assign say_it = false
  endif
-%}

{%- if value > 0 -%}
  <div class="rating-stars {{ class }}" data-rating="{{ value | round: 1 }}">
    <span class="rating-stars__row" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- for index in (1..scale_max) -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign threshold = index | minus: 0.5
        -%}
        {%- if value >= index -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'star', size: star_size, class: 'rating-stars__star rating-stars__star--full' %}
        {%- elsif value >= threshold -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'star-half', size: star_size, class: 'rating-stars__star rating-stars__star--half' %}
        {%- else -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'star', size: star_size, class: 'rating-stars__star rating-stars__star--empty' %}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </span>

    {%- if say_it -%}
      <span class="visually-hidden">
        {{- 'products.product.rating_html' | t: rating: value, max: scale_max -}}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
